    "label": "th:MainDistDep",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For any forecaster ... and any function $\\epsilon$ such that for all (Bernoulli) distributions ... there exists a constant $C \\geq 0$ with $\\E R_n \\leq C \\, \\epsilon(n)$, the following holds true: for all sets of $K \\geq 3$ Bernoulli distributions ... there exists a constant $D \\geq 0$ and an ordering ... such that $\\E r_n \\geq \\frac{\\Delta}{2} \\, e^{- D \\epsilon(n)}$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Paper's Delta is the minimal positive gap. Class: forecasters whose cumulative regret is bounded by C*eps(n)."
